const e="highland-games-piping-drumming-athletics",h=2026,t="The Evidence of the template names thechampionships.org.uk, which is the Scottish Schools Pipe Band Championships (SSPDT), a schools event that says it is not an RSPBA competition. So the content below is that event's rules, not RSPBA rules. Read: Rules & Eligibility, Enter, Event Info, Travel, Prizes, Contact, About, Home and the Endeavour Award pages. The rules page printed 'Closing date for entries is Friday 23 January 2026' (2026 edition); the home page now announces the 2027 Championships on Sunday 14 March 2027 at the William McIlvanney Campus, Kilmarnock, with no 2027 closing date yet. The 2027 date and venue are used, the 2026 closing date and the 2026 travel claim date are kept as the starting suggestion and marked 2026. The template groups Juvenile, Nov. Juvenile A and Nov. Juvenile B are printed on the page; the template groups Grade 1, Grade 2, Grade 3A, Grade 3B, Grade 4A and Grade 4B are not (they are RSPBA contest grades, not categories of this event), so they have no row. The page's categories Junior A, Junior B, Junior C, Quartets and Freestyle are not in the template and are named under 'other'. On Junior C the rules page says 'four parts of a march in any tempo' and the entry form says 'two 2-parted tunes in quick march time'; both are written. Not printed, so left empty: marks, points and rank scoring, how winners are chosen beyond the adjudicator panel, and the 2026 event date and venue. The names of winners (2026 Winners list) and the supporters list are not copied. The entry page names a staff member's e-mail for the Freestyle form; it is not copied. The H&S plan, catering menu and Travel Subsidy Form are linked as Documents. The privacy notice is linked.",a=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Scottish Schools Pipe Band Championships. Read these rules before you enter.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The Championships are for school and combined schools pipe bands. They are on {{ChampionshipsDate}} at {{Venue}}. They are not an RSPBA competition and are not run under RSPBA rules.","Notes":["Incomplete entry forms are not accepted. Please read the full rules and eligibility before you fill in the form.","All data in the entry form is shared with the event organiser.","Closing date for entries (2026 edition): {{EntryClosingDate}}."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Championships began in 2013. Their aims are to encourage the forming of new school pipe bands and give an entry level taste of competition, to celebrate Scotland's musical tradition and the talent of young people, and to show the range of the pipes and drums with other instruments.","The Championships are for full school or combined schools' pipe bands, not the mini band format usually seen in indoor competitions. They are also open to school pipe bands from outside Scotland.","The Scottish Schools Pipes and Drums Trust (SSPDT) organises the Championships on its own, with the support of the Royal Scottish Pipe Band Association (RSPBA). They are not an RSPBA competition and are not run under RSPBA rules.","There are eight categories. They give a place for top level competition and a friendly, encouraging place for school pipe bands with little or no competing experience.","Open to RSPBA-registered schools and bands only: Juvenile, Novice Juvenile 'A' and Novice Juvenile 'B'.","Open to schools and bands that are not registered with the RSPBA, and not open to RSPBA-registered schools or bands: Junior 'A', Junior 'B', Junior 'C' and Quartets.","Open to all participants in any of the above categories: the Freestyle competition. Freestyle entries are warmly encouraged from all schools that enter a band or quartet, whether or not they are RSPBA-registered.","Schools should choose the category or grade that suits them best and enter into the spirit of the event. Prizes are graded to encourage established bands to be ambitious.","The Championships are an indoor competition.","SSPDT supports school pipe bands that can last. Bands formed only to compete at the Championships, with no plan to continue, are not encouraged.","Members of the press and TV are present. If a player does not want their image used in press or TV coverage, complete, sign and return the consent form in advance."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["All pupils must be in full time education at their school at the time of the Championships.","No pupil may play in more than one of the competing pipe bands or piping quartets.","One adult instructor may play in all categories. In the Freestyle Musical Ensemble category, one adult, as conductor or leader, may take part. No other adult players are allowed.","If a school cannot enter a pipe band because it lacks players, a combined schools' pipe band may compete, if all the players are from schools (primary or secondary) in the same education authority.","If a pupil can play for both a school pipe band and a combined schools' pipe band, the school pipe band has priority, unless the head teacher gives permission to do otherwise. A pupil cannot play in both bands.","Players in combined schools' pipe bands and piping quartets must attend schools within the same education authority.","School pupils who are already registered with an RSPBA-registered school or combined schools pipe band may play only with that pipe band. Any school pipe band that has a player registered with the RSPBA must play in its Juvenile, Novice Juvenile 'A' or Novice Juvenile 'B' category of registration."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Enter online. The entry form has four steps and can be saved and continued later. The entrant confirms they have read the full rules and eligibility. Incomplete entries are not accepted.","Give the name of the school or combined schools (band, quartet or Freestyle ensemble) and the competition entered: Pipe Band Junior C, Junior A, Junior B, Juvenile, Novice Juvenile A or Novice Juvenile B; Quartet; or Freestyle.","Give the Local Education Authority, and for combined schools the list of all schools represented.","Give the main contact: name, role (for example tutor or head teacher), address, e-mail and telephone number.","Give the name and e-mail of the piping instructor. Also name every band, quartet and Freestyle ensemble, with its competition category, that your piping and drumming instructors help on the day, so that performance times do not clash.","Confirm that you have read the playing requirements for the categories entered, and give the names of the tunes.","Give the name of the adult contestant, if any. An adult Pipe Major may play in a band or quartet. An adult leader or conductor may take part in a Freestyle ensemble.","Give the total number of pupil pipers, snare drummers, bass drummers and tenor drummers (in a Freestyle ensemble: the number of pipers, drummers and other instrumentalists).","Give the names and RSPBA grades of all RSPBA-registered pupils, and the name of their band.","Write a short account of your band, quartet or Freestyle ensemble. Quartets that need help to start a pipe band can say so.","Name the adult who is responsible for your classroom on the day: name, role, e-mail, telephone and contact address.","Say if any band members or adults have restricted mobility and need help with the stairs.","Give the name and address of the organisation the prize money should be paid to, if you win a prize.","Freestyle entrants also complete the Freestyle Technical Requirements and Stage Plan form (print it, fill it in by hand, and upload it with the entry form or e-mail it). It is best to send it as early as possible, but it can be sent closer to the date.","Entries close on {{EntryClosingDate}} (2026 edition). Any change made before the competition must be told to the organisers.","Freestyle entries are taken first come first served, because the Freestyle competition is planned to run for no more than half the day.","On arrival, each band registers its attendance at Reception. On departure, each band checks out at Reception."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Entry Fee","Items":["Entry fee: {{EntryFee}}"]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["The next Championships are on {{ChampionshipsDate}}.","Closing date for entries (2026 edition): {{EntryClosingDate}}.","Travel expenses must be claimed by {{TravelClaimDeadline}} (2026 edition)."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The venue is {{Venue}}.","The organiser is at {{SSPDTAddress}}."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Players in a Pipe Band","Items":["A pipe band must have at least six pipers, two snare drummers and one bass drummer.","A band with fewer than these numbers is disqualified.","The most players in a band is 25."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Awards","Items":["Juvenile: {{PrizesJuvenile}}.","Novice Juvenile A: {{PrizesNoviceJuvenileA}}. Novice Juvenile B: {{PrizesNoviceJuvenileB}}.","Junior A and Junior B: {{PrizesJuniorAB}}. Junior C: {{PrizesJuniorC}}.","Quartets: {{PrizesQuartets}}.","Freestyle: {{PrizesFreestyle}}. Half of the Freestyle prize money goes to the pipe band for its own use and half goes to the school music department. If the performers belong to combined schools in one local authority area, all the prize money goes to the combined schools pipe band.","Eilidh MacLeod Endeavour Award: {{PrizeEndeavourAward}}. One exceptional band each year gets the award for going beyond the circle: community contribution, inclusion and diversity, enthusiasm and camaraderie, innovation, perseverance and resilience. A band applies by telling its story.","Prizes must be claimed within one month of the competition date.","Schools that cannot stay for prize giving, because of a long journey, should name a representative to collect any prize and give their steward a forwarding school contact name and address."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Arrangements on the Day","Items":["Band members wear the uniform that their school has set for the Championships.","Shoes with metal pieces on the sole or heel must be covered with jaffa tape to protect the flooring. Jaffa tape is available at Reception.","Each school gets a steward on arrival. The steward meets the pipe major, instructor or adult supervisor at Reception, takes the band to its classroom, explains fire drills, shows the facilities, makes sure band members complete the band sheets (name, school, age, gender, piper or drummer), explains the programme (playing times and competition hall locations), takes the band to the competition hall in good time for each performance, and sees the band off at the end of the day.","Each school gets a classroom for the day. There are no separate changing rooms for girls and boys.","Each band names a responsible adult (parent or teacher) to supervise the classroom. A supervising adult must be there at all times.","Before leaving, the responsible adult tells Reception and waits for a member of the organising committee to inspect and approve the classroom.","Keep classrooms neat and tidy. Do not move or tamper with school furniture or equipment. Smoking, alcohol, food, soft drinks and aerosols are strictly forbidden in classrooms. Stewards provide rubbish bags.","Any damage is charged to the visiting band or school. Past damage, graffiti and litter forced the Championships to change venue.","Bands and quartets do not have to march in or out of the hall, but all groups should come in and leave in an organised way. First impressions are important.","Catering: breakfast, lunch and snacks are on sale in the school cafeteria, with gluten-free and vegan choices. No alcohol is allowed on site.","Lost property: hand in and collect it at Reception. After the Championships, write to {{SSPDTOffice}}."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["The pipe band competitions are judged by RSPBA-approved adjudicators. Where it suits, the adjudication team is the same as for RSPBA major championships: two piping adjudicators, one drumming adjudicator and one ensemble adjudicator.","The Quartet Piping and Freestyle Musical Ensemble competitions are judged by a panel of adjudicators."]},{"Key":"payments","Title":"Travel Help","Items":["SSPDT helps bands with travel costs. To qualify for a travel subsidy, a band must be a Scottish state school, travel as a group by public transport or private coach hire, and be based more than 100 miles from the venue. Receipts or invoices must be given.","Band award: {{TravelSubsidyBands}}","A quartet must be a Scottish state school, travel as a group (public transport is encouraged), be based more than 100 miles from the venue, and give receipts or invoices where they apply. Quartet award: {{TravelSubsidyQuartets}}","To claim, download and fill in the Travel Subsidy Form and e-mail it to {{SSPDTOffice}}. Travel expenses must be claimed by {{TravelClaimDeadline}} (2026 edition). No award is made without receipts and invoices, where they apply."]},{"Key":"reporting","Title":"Results","Items":["Winners are announced on the day and posted on the Championships web site."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Categories the Template Does Not Carry","Items":["Junior 'A', 'B' and 'C' pipe bands (not RSPBA-registered): the school or combined schools decides its category and, if needed, explains the choice to the organisers, who may place a band in a different category. These bands may include pupils registered with RSPBA community pipe bands, if no more than one third of the pipers (including the pipe major) are registered no higher than Grade 3 (the pipe major may be at any level), only one snare drummer is registered no higher than Grade 3, and the names and grades of all RSPBA-registered pupils are on the entry form. Junior A plays two 2-parted 2/4 marches or one 4-parted march, two 2-parted strathspeys or one 4-parted strathspey, and two 2-parted reels or one 4-parted reel. Junior B plays four 2-parted 2/4 marches, or two 4-parted 2/4 marches. Junior C plays four parts of a march in any tempo (the entry form says any two 2-parted tunes in quick march time, 2/4, 3/4, 4/4, 6/8 or 9/8). Tunes are of the band's own choice; a list of recommended tunes is on the RSPBA web site.","Piping Quartet: open to schools that cannot form a pipe band. Four school pupils (or three pupils and one adult instructor if a fourth pupil is not possible). The pupils must not have played with a participating pipe band. A school or band that has entered a band category may not enter a quartet. Combined schools' quartets use pupils from the same education authority and should not include a player from a school that enters a quartet itself. There is no limit to the number of years a pupil may compete in a school quartet. Play two 2-parted 2/4 marches or one 4-parted 2/4 march, of own choice.","Freestyle Musical Ensemble: open to all schools or combined schools that have entered other Championships competitions. One category. A pipe band performing an innovative concert-style medley, or a mixed ensemble of pipers and other instrumentalists. Each school may enter only one Freestyle ensemble. At least six players, of whom at least two are pipers and one a drummer (not necessarily a pipe band drummer), at most 25 players on stage plus 2 pupils on a drum kit and keyboard on raised platforms at the rear. One adult only, as conductor or leader. 8 minutes to set up and at most 5 minutes of playing. Music is the school's choice, but the piping and drumming should stand out. Judged on musicianship, harmony, originality, innovation, musical interpretation, presentation, rhythm, ensemble, vitality and technical proficiency. A stage plan is sent to entrants before the event. A drum kit, a keyboard, a guitar amplifier and a bass amplifier are on stage; bring your own other instruments, pedals, leads and drum sticks. All instruments are line checked in the 8 minute change-over. Sound engineers are on hand all day, but there is no sound check in advance.","The Eilidh MacLeod Endeavour Award is open to bands, not to a competition class. See Prizes."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Rules & Eligibility (Scottish Schools Pipe Band Championships)","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/enter-championships/rules-eligibility/"},{"Title":"Event Info","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/event-info/"},{"Title":"Prizes","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/prizes/"},{"Title":"Travel","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/getting-there/"},{"Title":"Freestyle Technical Requirements & Stage Plan 2026","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Freestyle-Technical-Requirements-Stage-Plan-2026.pdf"},{"Title":"Championships 2026 Catering Menu","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Championships-2026-Catering-Menu.pdf"},{"Title":"Safety Management Plan 2026","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/SSPBC-Safety-Management-Plan-2026.docx"},{"Title":"Travel Subsidy Form 2026","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Travel-Subsidy-Form-2026.docx"},{"Title":"Privacy Notice","Url":"https://thechampionships.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/SSPDT-Privacy-Notice-January-2019.pdf"}]}`),n=[],o=[{AgeGroup:"Juvenile",Source:"Rules & Eligibility page Juvenile Pipe Band Competition; Enter The Championships page playing requirements",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Play one March, Strathspey and Reel, each with a minimum of four parts."],Rules:["Band grade: Juvenile Grade."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Play one March, Strathspey and Reel, each with a minimum of four parts.

## Rules
- Band grade: Juvenile Grade.`},{AgeGroup:"Nov. Juvenile A",Source:"Rules & Eligibility page Novice Juvenile 'A' Pipe Band Competition; Enter The Championships page playing requirements",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Play two 2-parted 2/4 Marches or one 4-parted 2/4 March, and two 2-parted Strathspeys or one 4-parted Strathspey, and two 2-parted Reels or one 4-parted Reel.","All tunes are chosen from the list of prescribed tunes on the RSPBA web site. They may include parts one and two of the four-parted tunes."],Rules:["Band grade: Novice Juvenile or Grade 4 'A' Grade."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Play two 2-parted 2/4 Marches or one 4-parted 2/4 March, and two 2-parted Strathspeys or one 4-parted Strathspey, and two 2-parted Reels or one 4-parted Reel.
- All tunes are chosen from the list of prescribed tunes on the RSPBA web site. They may include parts one and two of the four-parted tunes.

## Rules
- Band grade: Novice Juvenile or Grade 4 'A' Grade.`},{AgeGroup:"Nov. Juvenile B",Source:"Rules & Eligibility page Novice Juvenile 'B' Pipe Band Competition; Enter The Championships page playing requirements",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Play four 2-parted 2/4 Marches.","All tunes are chosen from the list of prescribed tunes on the RSPBA web site. They may include parts one and two of the four-parted tunes."],Rules:["Band grade: Novice Juvenile or Grade 4 'B' Grade."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Play four 2-parted 2/4 Marches.
- All tunes are chosen from the list of prescribed tunes on the RSPBA web site. They may include parts one and two of the four-parted tunes.

## Rules
- Band grade: Novice Juvenile or Grade 4 'B' Grade.`}],i=[{Title:"Pipe Band Competition",Source:"Rules & Eligibility page Playing Formation",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["All pipe bands play in a half circle facing the adjudicators. Drummers can be inside the half circle with the pipers, or behind the pipers in the half circle."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- All pipe bands play in a half circle facing the adjudicators. Drummers can be inside the half circle with the pipers, or behind the pipers in the half circle.`}],r=[],s=[{Key:"ChampionshipsDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date of the next Championships",Value:"2027-03-14",Source:"Home page (Sunday 14 March 2027)"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Event venue",Value:{Name:"William McIlvanney Campus",Address:"",City:"Kilmarnock",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Home page (the 2027 Championships are at the William McIlvanney Campus, Kilmarnock)"},{Key:"EntryClosingDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Closing date for entries (2026 edition)",Value:"2026-01-23",Source:"Rules & Eligibility page (Closing date for entries is Friday 23 January 2026). Printed for the 2026 edition; the 2027 date is not yet on the site."},{Key:"TravelClaimDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to claim travel expenses (2026 edition)",Value:"2026-03-31",Source:"Travel page (claimed by 31st March, 2026)"},{Key:"EntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee",Value:"No entry fee on the day. Donations are welcome because the event is organised by a charity.",Source:"Event Info page (Fee)"},{Key:"PrizesJuvenile",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes: Juvenile",Value:"1st 500 pounds; 2nd 400; 3rd 300; 4th 200; 5th 100",Source:"Prizes page"},{Key:"PrizesNoviceJuvenileA",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes: Novice Juvenile A",Value:"1st 400 pounds; 2nd 300; 3rd 250; 4th 200; 5th 100",Source:"Prizes page"},{Key:"PrizesNoviceJuvenileB",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes: Novice Juvenile B",Value:"1st 400 pounds; 2nd 300; 3rd 250; 4th 200; 5th 100",Source:"Prizes page"},{Key:"PrizesJuniorAB",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes: Junior A and Junior B",Value:"1st 350 pounds; 2nd 250; 3rd 200; 4th 100; 5th 50",Source:"Prizes page"},{Key:"PrizesJuniorC",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes: Junior C (formerly Debut)",Value:"1st 300 pounds; 2nd 200; 3rd 150; 4th 100; 5th 50",Source:"Prizes page"},{Key:"PrizesQuartets",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes: Quartets",Value:"1st 300 pounds; 2nd 200; 3rd 150; 4th 100; 5th 50",Source:"Prizes page"},{Key:"PrizesFreestyle",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes: Freestyle (new prize amounts for 2025)",Value:"1st 1500 pounds; 2nd 1400; 3rd 1300; 4th 1200; 5th 1100",Source:"Prizes page"},{Key:"PrizeEndeavourAward",Kind:"prize",Label:"Eilidh MacLeod Endeavour Award",Value:"1000 pounds (doubled from 500 pounds)",Source:"Prizes page; Eilidh MacLeod Endeavour Award page"},{Key:"TravelSubsidyBands",Kind:"text",Label:"Travel subsidy for bands",Value:"50% of costs up to 500 pounds. Exceptional cases for rural or island bands: up to 1500 pounds.",Source:"Travel page (2026)"},{Key:"TravelSubsidyQuartets",Kind:"text",Label:"Travel subsidy for quartets",Value:"20p per mile for fuel, or accommodation or public transport costs, up to 400 pounds.",Source:"Travel page (2026)"},{Key:"SSPDTOffice",Kind:"contact",Label:"Scottish Schools Pipes and Drums Trust (SSPDT)",Value:{Name:"The Scottish Schools Pipe Band Championships (SSPDT)",Role:"Organiser",Phone:"0131 510 8384",WhatsApp:"",Email:"info@sspdt.org.uk"},Source:"Contact page"},{Key:"SSPDTAddress",Kind:"address",Label:"Organiser address",Value:{Name:"The Scottish Schools Pipe Band Championships",Address:"Rm 1, Thistle Court, 1-2 Thistle Street",City:"Edinburgh EH2 1DD",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Contact page"},{Key:"SponsorshipContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Sponsorship enquiries",Value:{Name:"SSPDT administration",Role:"Request the Sponsorship Package",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"admin@sspdt.org.uk"},Source:"Home page"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"Notices printed on the site",Value:[{Date:"2027-03-14",Title:"2027 Championships",Text:"The 2027 Championships are on Sunday 14 March 2027 at the William McIlvanney Campus, Kilmarnock.",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/"},{Date:"",Title:"2026 entries closed",Text:"Entry to the 2026 Championships is closed. The closing date was Friday 23 January 2026.",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/enter-championships/"},{Date:"",Title:"Eilidh MacLeod Endeavour Award prize doubled",Text:"The Eilidh MacLeod Endeavour Award, for a band that goes beyond the circle with community contribution, inclusion, enthusiasm, innovation or resilience, now carries 1000 pounds, up from 500 pounds.",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/enter-championships/endeavour-award-nomination/"},{Date:"",Title:"New Freestyle prizes",Text:"Freestyle prize amounts are new from 2025. See the prize list.",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/prizes/"},{Date:"",Title:"Junior C",Text:"Junior C was introduced in 2024 for inexperienced bands with little or no previous competing experience, including development bands of schools with other RSPBA-registered players.",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/enter-championships/rules-eligibility/"}],Source:"Home page; Rules & Eligibility page; Prizes page; Eilidh MacLeod Endeavour Award page"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, categories, eligibility, number of players, playing requirements and adjudication are those printed on the Rules & Eligibility page of the Scottish Schools Pipe Band Championships (organised by the Scottish Schools Pipes and Drums Trust). The page says the Championships are not an RSPBA competition and are not run under RSPBA rules.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules page",Source:"Rules & Eligibility - The Championships",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/enter-championships/rules-eligibility/"},{Claim:"Entry form fields, arrival and classroom arrangements, fee, travel subsidy, prizes, contact and next date come from the Enter, Event Info, Travel, Prizes, Contact and Home pages of the same site.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own web site",Source:"thechampionships.org.uk",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/"},{Claim:"The site prints no marking scheme, no marks, no points and no rank scoring. Nothing was written from general knowledge.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own web site",Source:"thechampionships.org.uk",Url:"https://thechampionships.org.uk/"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,h as Year,d as default};
